DOLE Presenter: a strong performance. As of July 2026, we have maintained a 99% disposition rate, resulting in approximately 6.76 billion in monetary awards benefiting more than 99,000 workers. For actual strikes and lockouts, we have

asr-000171
00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:16.720
DOLE Presenter: disposed 80% as of August, involving approximately

asr-000172
00:19:16.720 --> 00:19:20.460
DOLE Presenter: 35.19 million in settlements, benefiting 284 workers.

asr-000173
00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.040
DOLE Presenter: For 2027,

asr-000176
00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.900
DOLE Presenter: we will continue to pursue a 100% disposition target.

asr-000177
00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:27.900
DOLE Presenter: For voluntary arbitration, we have settled 60%,

asr-000178
00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:32.060
DOLE Presenter: which generated around 2.96 billion in settlements,

asr-000179
00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.920
DOLE Presenter: benefiting 1,458 workers.

asr-000180
00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:40.460
DOLE Presenter: For 2027, we propose to sustain all of our targets under case management.

asr-000181
00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:45.160
DOLE Presenter: For fiscal year 2027, under the National Expenditure Program,

asr-000182
00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:48.160
DOLE Presenter: the Department of Labor and Employment has been allocated

asr-000183
00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:52.000
DOLE Presenter: a total budget of 47.057 billion pesos.

asr-000184
00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.920
DOLE Presenter: This will support the operations of the department,

asr-000185
00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:59.280
DOLE Presenter: its six attached agencies, and 17 regional offices nationwide.

asr-000186
00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.420
DOLE Presenter: This figure excludes automatic appropriations,

asr-000187
00:20:02.600 --> 00:20:06.060
DOLE Presenter: totaling 668 million broken down as follows.

asr-000188
00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:10.000
DOLE Presenter: 668.058 million for retirement and life insurance premiums

asr-000189
00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:14.580
DOLE Presenter: and 375,000 for special voluntary arbitration fund

asr-000190
00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:17.080
DOLE Presenter: under the National Conciliation and Mediation Board.

asr-000191
00:20:17.080 --> 00:20:19.780
DOLE Presenter: Looking at the budget distribution,

asr-000192
00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:25.120
DOLE Presenter: Dole Proper and TESDA account for nearly 90% of the department's total budget.

asr-000193
00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:29.780
DOLE Presenter: Dole Proper receives the largest share at 20.955 billion,

asr-000194
00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:33.720
DOLE Presenter: supporting core programs, field operations, and frontline services.

asr-000195
00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:37.480
DOLE Presenter: TESDA follows with 20.895 billion,

asr-000196
00:20:37.860 --> 00:20:41.160
DOLE Presenter: reflecting our strong investment in technical vocational training

asr-000197
00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:42.520
DOLE Presenter: and workforce upskilling.

asr-000198
00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:45.460
DOLE Presenter: The remaining is shared among the attached agencies,

asr-000199
00:20:45.960 --> 00:20:47.060
DOLE Presenter: PRC at 2.694 billion,

asr-000200
00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:51.460
DOLE Presenter: NLRC at 1.733 billion,

asr-000201
00:20:51.960 --> 00:20:54.400
DOLE Presenter: NWPC at 369 million,

asr-000202
00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.160
DOLE Presenter: NCMB at 332 million,

asr-000203
00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:00.040
DOLE Presenter: and ILS at 79 million.

asr-000204
00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:05.920
DOLE Presenter: Fiscal year 2027 NEP of 47.057 billion

asr-000205
00:21:05.920 --> 00:21:14.140
DOLE Presenter: is 14.116 billion lower than the 2026 GAA of 61.173 billion.

asr-000206
00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:16.140
DOLE Presenter: However, it is 2.675 billion higher

asr-000207
00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:22.780
DOLE Presenter: than the fiscal year 2026 NEP of 44.382 billion.

asr-000208
00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:28.300
DOLE Presenter: Overall, the fiscal year 2027 proposal shows an increase from the previous NEP,

asr-000209
00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:31.260
DOLE Presenter: but a significant reduction from the current GAA.

asr-000210
00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:37.320
DOLE Presenter: The department originally proposed 70.426 billion for fiscal year 2027

asr-000211
00:21:37.320 --> 00:21:39.680
DOLE Presenter: to address key labour sector priorities.

asr-000212
00:21:39.680 --> 00:21:44.780
DOLE Presenter: However, the 2027 NEP provides only 47.57 billion,

asr-000213
00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:46.680
DOLE Presenter: a 23.368 billion,

asr-000214
00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:51.820
DOLE Presenter: or a 33.18% reduction from the original proposal.

asr-000215
00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:57.540
DOLE Presenter: Overall, the recommended budget for DoLE decreased by 14.116 billion,

asr-000216
00:21:57.540 --> 00:21:59.280
DOLE Presenter: or 23.08%,

asr-000217
00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.880
DOLE Presenter: compared with the 2026 GAA.

asr-000218
00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:08.480
DOLE Presenter: This reduction is primarily due to lower budget allocations for DoLE, NCMB, NLRC, and TESDA.

asr-000219
00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:16.840
DOLE Presenter: Conversely, the recommended budgets for ILS, NWPC, and PRC increased compared with their 2026 GAA levels.

asr-000220
00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:18.560
DOLE Presenter: Compared with the 2027 proposed budget

asr-000221
00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:21.300
DOLE Presenter: compared with the 2027 proposed budget submitted to the DBM,

asr-000222
00:22:21.300 --> 00:22:22.420
DOLE Presenter: the 2027 NEP

asr-000223
00:22:22.420 --> 00:22:27.640
DOLE Presenter: the 2027 NEP reflects a net decrease of 23.368 billion,

asr-000224
00:22:27.640 --> 00:22:31.280
DOLE Presenter: or 33.18% in total funding.

asr-000225
00:22:31.280 --> 00:22:36.120
DOLE Presenter: The 2027 NEP of 47.57 billion,

asr-000226
00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:39.780
