00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:46.220
DOLE Presenter: 8.443 billion is

asr-000229
00:22:46.220 --> 00:22:46.720
DOLE Presenter: allocated

asr-000230
00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:52.500
DOLE Presenter: to personnel services, and 525 million is allocated to capital outlay.

asr-000231
00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:58.140
DOLE Presenter: While the overall budget reflects significant reductions, personnel services increased by

asr-000232
00:22:58.140 --> 00:23:04.320
DOLE Presenter: 0.021 billion from last year. The increase also covers the salaries and benefits of newly hired

asr-000233
00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:09.280
DOLE Presenter: and promoted employees, field non-permanent positions, and terminal leave benefits of

asr-000234
00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:16.320
DOLE Presenter: mandatory retirees. For maintenance and other operating expenses, the 2026 NEP amounted to

asr-000235
00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:25.820
DOLE Presenter: 35.05 billion, which increased significantly to 51.91 billion under the 2026 GAA. For 2027,

asr-000236
00:23:26.140 --> 00:23:36.180
DOLE Presenter: the proposed NEP stands at 38.10 billion. Compared with the 2026 GAA, the 2027 NEP is lower by 13.82

asr-000237
00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:42.800
DOLE Presenter: billion. However, compared with the 2026 NEP, it reflects an increase of 3.44 billion.

asr-000238
00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:46.240
DOLE Presenter: The reduction from the 2026 GAA is

asr-000239
00:23:46.240 --> 00:23:52.740
DOLE Presenter: mainly due to lower funding requirements for key programs, including TUPAD, DILP, STEP,

asr-000240
00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:58.640
