asr-005873
06:31:31.790 --> 06:31:31.810
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair and Mr. Secretary, Director General, and the DoLE family.

asr-005874
06:31:32.430 --> 06:31:34.750
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So actually, I'm here today to help this...

asr-005875
06:31:34.750 --> 06:31:35.450
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Good afternoon, Mr. Chair and Mr. Secretary, Director General, and the DoLE family.

asr-005876
06:31:35.470 --> 06:31:43.270
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: To help this committee give the department and the whole DoLE family what it needs to effectively perform its mandate under the labor code.

asr-005877
06:31:44.050 --> 06:31:50.650
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, my first question is really about the visitorial and enforcement powers of the DoLE.

asr-005878
06:31:51.330 --> 06:32:05.270
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Because as a labor law practitioner before entering politics, I saw that there are some cases wherein if we just fully fund or support or give enough funding for the enforcement power of the DoLE,

asr-005881
06:32:05.970 --> 06:32:07.630
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: may mga cases po sana na

asr-005882
06:32:07.830 --> 06:32:10.410
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: natulungan po talaga natin fully yung mga laborers.

asr-005883
06:32:10.590 --> 06:32:12.110
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And one of those cases is

asr-005884
06:32:12.110 --> 06:32:13.650
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: the Manggagawa sa Komunikasyon ng Pilipinas

asr-005885
06:32:13.650 --> 06:32:17.690
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: versus PLDT,

asr-005886
06:32:17.690 --> 06:32:20.410
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: which was decided in February 2024.

asr-005887
06:32:21.010 --> 06:32:30.430
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, what happened in 2016 was the Department of Labor and Employment inspected the company pursuant to its Article 128 power.

asr-005888
06:32:30.930 --> 06:32:31.330
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And in January 2018, the Secretary of Labor ordered the regularization of the Inspector General's license,

asr-005889
06:32:31.330 --> 06:32:36.970
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And in January 2018, the Secretary of Labor ordered the regularization of the contracted

asr-005890
06:32:36.970 --> 06:32:37.970
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: workers.

asr-005891
06:32:37.970 --> 06:32:42.310
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So there was about 7,344 of them on the final count.

asr-005892
06:32:42.310 --> 06:32:47.690
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And I think this was one of the largest regularizations that happened in our country.

asr-005893
06:32:47.690 --> 06:32:56.030
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So the court set aside some of the categories.

asr-005894
06:32:56.030 --> 06:33:01.910
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So they regularized some, but they also set aside some of the categories such as janitorial,

asr-005895
06:33:01.910 --> 06:33:05.930
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: IT, back office, call centers, and the like.

asr-005896
06:33:05.930 --> 06:33:10.650
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So these were thousands of workers, not because the DOLE was wrong, but because the labor

asr-005897
06:33:10.650 --> 06:33:17.130
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: law compliance officers had interviewed, in the court's words, not more than 1,000 individuals

asr-005898
06:33:17.130 --> 06:33:21.130
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: and applied the findings to 7,344.

asr-005899
06:33:21.130 --> 06:33:25.970
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So the court wrote that conclusions based on sampling or probability in its decision

asr-005900
06:33:25.970 --> 06:33:29.610
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: should not be considered substantial evidence.

asr-005901
06:33:29.610 --> 06:33:35.250
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So my question is, today, how many inspectors are actually on paper, and how many of the

asr-005902
06:33:35.250 --> 06:33:39.470
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: inspectors are actually on the field deployed and doing their inspection powers?

asr-005903
06:33:39.470 --> 06:33:48.920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: A while ago, Your Honor, we were really confronted with that continuing challenge of lack of

asr-005904
06:33:48.920 --> 06:33:52.960
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: manpower insofar as the labor inspectorate is concerned.

asr-005905
06:33:52.960 --> 06:33:56.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yung inabutan ko, dapat daw ay 1,210

asr-005906
06:33:56.160 --> 06:33:57.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ang sa buong Pilipinas,

asr-005907
06:33:57.160 --> 06:34:02.400
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: subalit sa ngayon ay wala pang 700.

asr-005908
06:34:02.400 --> 06:34:09.820
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Dumaan sila sa isang masusing eksaminasyon, subalit kahit

asr-005909
06:34:09.820 --> 06:34:15.920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: mabuo yung 1,210, that would not be sufficient

asr-005910
06:34:15.920 --> 06:34:16.920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: to address that continuing concern.

asr-005911
06:34:16.920 --> 06:34:25.800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Kulang talaga. Hindi kaya, hindi lamang sa mga pribadong establishments

asr-005912
06:34:25.800 --> 06:34:26.800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: kundi pati government projects.

asr-005913
06:34:27.160 --> 06:34:28.320
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ang nag-i-inspect din po noon, DOLE.

asr-005914
06:34:28.320 --> 06:34:30.940
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So hindi talaga kayang punuan o

asr-005915
06:34:30.940 --> 06:34:32.380
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So hindi talaga kayang

asr-005916
06:34:32.380 --> 06:34:38.320
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: punuan o gampanan. So as to the details of, I agree with you,

asr-005917
06:34:38.320 --> 06:34:41.660
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: yung kaso sigurong iyon ay kung nagkaroon ng tama at

asr-005918
06:34:41.660 --> 06:34:45.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: appropriate labor inspection,

asr-005919
06:34:45.200 --> 06:34:46.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Article 128

asr-005920
06:34:46.200 --> 06:34:47.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ay siguro

asr-005921
06:34:47.200 --> 06:34:48.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: may

asr-005922
06:34:48.200 --> 06:34:49.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: sapat na

asr-005925
06:34:51.200 --> 06:34:52.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: compliance

asr-005926
06:34:52.200 --> 06:34:53.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: kasi na-correct

asr-005927
06:34:53.200 --> 06:34:54.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: naman po iyan eh.

asr-005928
06:34:54.200 --> 06:34:55.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: But as to the

asr-005929
06:34:55.200 --> 06:34:56.200
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: other details,

asr-005930
06:34:56.200 --> 06:34:57.000
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: is BLE here

asr-005931
06:34:57.000 --> 06:34:57.980
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: o sino

asr-005932
06:34:57.980 --> 06:34:58.980
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: sasagot?

asr-005933
06:34:58.980 --> 06:34:59.980
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes.

asr-005934
06:34:59.980 --> 06:35:03.420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Usec Legargo, would you like to contribute something with permission of the Chair?

asr-005935
06:35:03.420 --> 06:35:10.340
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: With the kind permission of the Honorable Secretary, the Honorable Members of the Committee,

asr-005936
06:35:11.600 --> 06:35:19.520
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Congressman, ibe-verify pa namin sa Court of Appeals and Supreme Court

asr-005937
06:35:19.520 --> 06:35:27.000
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: because it has already been decided, and then we will give you the final outcome.

asr-005938
06:35:27.000 --> 06:35:36.860
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: As for the interview, ginagawa namin na lahat na hindi na random ang interview

asr-005939
06:35:36.860 --> 06:35:41.260
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: para siguradong makuha namin lahat.

asr-005940
06:35:41.860 --> 06:35:42.260
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Thank you.

asr-005941
06:35:43.400 --> 06:35:49.720
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Sa bagong Department Order No. 238.

asr-005942
06:35:50.420 --> 06:35:51.380
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Thank you.

asr-005943
06:35:52.500 --> 06:35:55.240
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Thank you, Usec and Mr. Secretary.

asr-005944
06:35:55.640 --> 06:35:56.720
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, right now,

asr-005945
06:35:56.720 --> 06:36:02.340
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: what does an inspection now have to look like to survive judicial review?

asr-005946
06:36:02.720 --> 06:36:06.600
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Because, given the case, given the requirements of the Supreme Court,

asr-005947
06:36:07.480 --> 06:36:11.320
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: how many interviews, how many inspector days,

asr-005948
06:36:11.320 --> 06:36:18.780
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: for example, an establishment similar to the establishment in the Supreme Court case?

asr-005949
06:36:19.160 --> 06:36:22.780
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: As an estimate, please.

asr-005950
06:36:24.040 --> 06:36:27.960
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Our current inspection is,

asr-005951
06:36:28.100 --> 06:36:29.540
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: ngayon ay tripartite.

asr-005952
06:36:30.920 --> 06:36:36.560
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: So that way we can be sure na represented lahat ng mga sectors.

asr-005953
06:36:39.140 --> 06:36:41.760
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Employers, workers at saka government.

asr-005954
06:36:42.980 --> 06:36:44.340
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-005955
06:36:44.820 --> 06:36:46.040
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, now on to the budget.

asr-005956
06:36:46.540 --> 06:36:53.640
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, under the NEP, the labor laws compliance is at around ₱877 million.

asr-005957
06:36:54.280 --> 06:36:56.820
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, what is the ideal figure?

asr-005958
06:36:56.820 --> 06:36:59.060
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: What is the ideal peso figure?

asr-005959
06:36:59.700 --> 06:37:04.060
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: For every large establishment, inspectors, the evidence the Supreme Court now requires.

asr-005960
06:37:19.900 --> 06:37:26.960
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: Actually, ang iniisip namin ay more or less 9,000 inspectors

asr-005961
06:37:26.960 --> 06:37:32.450
DOLE Undersecretary Felipe N. Egargo Jr.: para mahagip natin ang karamihan na establishments.

asr-005961-split-2
06:37:32.450 --> 06:37:35.680
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Opo, 8,000 ang kulang.

asr-005962
06:37:35.680 --> 06:37:43.030
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Actually, I ask these questions po just to emphasize how important it is to support and to fully fund

asr-005963
06:37:43.030 --> 06:37:44.890
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: the endeavors of the NEP.

asr-005964
06:37:44.890 --> 06:37:49.150
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, what is the objective of the NEP when it comes to the inspection and the Visitorial Enforcement Power?

asr-005965
06:37:49.150 --> 06:37:55.130
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Because enforcement power without manpower to prove the case is really not enough.

asr-005966
06:37:55.130 --> 06:37:59.170
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So, just to move on to another question.

asr-005967
06:37:59.170 --> 06:38:05.450
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Regarding po sa Bicol wage and the diesel shock,

asr-005968
06:38:05.450 --> 06:38:09.650
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: kasi currently ₱455 po yung minimum wage sa Bicol,

asr-005969
06:38:09.650 --> 06:38:13.050
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: around ₱11,830 sa isang buwan.

asr-005973
06:38:14.770 --> 06:38:19.570
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Pero doon sa dalawang buwan po this year, may dumoble po yung presyo ng diesel.

asr-005974
06:38:19.570 --> 06:38:23.650
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: May sariling patakaran po yung wage commission na pwedeng buksan ulit yung wage order

asr-005975
06:38:23.650 --> 06:38:27.870
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: kapag biglang tumaas po yung presyo ng, for example, petrolyo.

asr-005976
06:38:27.870 --> 06:38:32.010
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So yung question ko lang po, yung Region 5 po, RTWPB,

asr-005977
06:38:32.010 --> 06:38:40.610
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: did it formally assess whether a supervening condition existed after that fuel shock?

asr-005978
06:38:40.610 --> 06:38:48.610
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Your Honor, nandito ata yung Region 5.

asr-005979
06:38:51.860 --> 06:38:53.300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We have a new Region 5 director.

asr-005980
06:38:53.300 --> 06:39:17.150
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Si Director Panlilio, she just assumed office. Pero ilang araw ka na ba doon? Bago pa lang eh. Hindi pa siya nakaka-assume. So NWPC perhaps give input? Ah, go ahead.

asr-005981
06:39:17.150 --> 06:39:23.870
DOLE Region V Regional Director Geraldine M. Panlilio: With the permission po of our honorable Secretary, the Bicol Region, in consideration of the current

asr-005982
06:39:23.870 --> 06:39:42.620
DOLE Region V Regional Director Geraldine M. Panlilio: wage order na ₱455 po ang current minimum wage. Currently po, undergoing na kami, diretso na, mayroon na pong kino-conduct na wage deliberation para po ma-review na natin talagang kailangan na

asr-005983
06:39:42.620 --> 06:39:46.260
DOLE Region V Regional Director Geraldine M. Panlilio: because of the current situation. Thank you po.

asr-005983-split-2
06:39:47.420 --> 06:39:50.910
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Thank you very much po. So just another question

asr-005984
06:39:50.910 --> 06:39:53.230
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: regarding that so what does the wage commission

asr-005985
06:39:53.870 --> 06:39:58.990
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: need to make sure that when an extraordinary shock uh hits workers the mechanism already

asr-005986
06:39:58.990 --> 06:40:06.850
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: written into the rules of the wage commission can actually be used. Enough na rin po ba yung current po na?

asr-005986-split-2
06:40:06.850 --> 06:40:09.900
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: NWPC? Is she here? [unclear].

asr-005987
06:40:14.180 --> 06:40:33.810
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: Good afternoon, Your Honors. [unclear], nakalagay po sa guidelines ng minimum wage determination that the board, based on their assessment of the socioeconomic conditions,

asr-005988
06:40:33.810 --> 06:40:45.010
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: and if the wage order is not yet has reached its anniversary they have for the power to evaluate

asr-005989
06:40:45.010 --> 06:40:52.690
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: whether there exists and supervening condition or not but it has to go through the commission

asr-005990
06:40:52.690 --> 06:41:00.220
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: for affirmation even before they conduct a public hearing.

asr-005990-split-2
06:41:00.220 --> 06:41:04.430
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Okay po. So bale, just to reiterate the

asr-005991
06:41:05.310 --> 06:41:10.670
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: just to clarify lang din po the nwpc has what it needs to enforce and to

asr-005992
06:41:11.470 --> 06:41:14.400
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: operationalize po the rules that are already written in its ano.

asr-005992-split-2
06:41:14.400 --> 06:41:15.580
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: Yes, Mr. Chair.

asr-005992-split-3
06:41:15.580 --> 06:41:16.110
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Okay po.

asr-005993
06:41:17.150 --> 06:41:22.470
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: Thank you po. For the second tranche, kapagka ito ay

asr-005994
06:41:22.470 --> 06:41:29.270
NWPC Executive Director Maria Criselda Sy: na-approve na yung wage order, effective na po iyon. Hindi na po iyon mababago.

asr-005996
06:41:29.270 --> 06:41:34.780
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Okay, maraming salamat po. Actually iyon lang naman po yung mga katanungan ko, and gusto ko lang po sabihin na a labor law is

asr-005997
06:41:34.780 --> 06:41:37.480
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: only as strong as the department that enforces it.

asr-005998
06:41:37.480 --> 06:41:40.520
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: So I hope the department will tell this committee

asr-005999
06:41:40.520 --> 06:41:44.590
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: po, plainly what it needs to be restored to the budget.

asr-006000
06:41:44.590 --> 06:41:48.250
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: And I just want to manifest my full support for the department

asr-006001
06:41:48.250 --> 06:41:51.130
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: and all the Department of Labor and Employment family.

asr-006002
06:41:51.490 --> 06:41:52.310
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Thank you very much.

asr-006003
06:41:52.570 --> 06:41:53.630
Rep. Jan Franz Norbert Joselito A. Chan: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-006004
06:41:54.770 --> 06:41:56.810
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you, Representative Jan Chan.

asr-006005
06:41:57.930 --> 06:42:02.030
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Next on the list, of course, from the majority,

asr-006006
06:42:02.250 --> 06:42:04.410
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: of course, Representative Miro Kimbo.

asr-006007
06:42:08.400 --> 06:42:09.540
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Kasisimula ko pa lang eh.

asr-006008
06:42:10.960 --> 06:42:14.960
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Ha? Teka, parang sinimulan ninyo sa iyong pag-immediate na zero.

asr-006009
06:42:14.960 --> 06:42:16.900
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Baka kay Congressman Eli ninyo balak gawin iyon.

asr-006010
06:42:18.140 --> 06:42:19.020
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Hindi sa akin.

asr-006011
06:42:20.920 --> 06:42:23.780
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I'm tempted to give my time to Kong Eli

asr-006012
06:42:23.780 --> 06:42:25.760
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: so that I will have more time.

asr-006013
06:42:26.340 --> 06:42:27.960
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Because this is...

asr-006014
06:42:27.960 --> 06:42:30.160
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Well, anyway, magandang gabi po sa ating lahat.

asr-006015
06:42:31.100 --> 06:42:32.860
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Gabi na eh, 5:43 na dito.

asr-006016
06:42:32.980 --> 06:42:33.940
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: Gabi na ho sa amin iyan eh.

asr-006017
06:42:35.860 --> 06:42:37.460
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I think that, you know,

asr-006018
06:42:37.500 --> 06:42:38.380
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: while the function of the department

asr-006019
06:42:38.380 --> 06:42:41.740
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: of labor is to protect workers,

asr-006020
06:42:42.180 --> 06:42:44.320
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: but on the flip side,

asr-006021
06:42:44.640 --> 06:42:47.580
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: much of the programs that have also been very impactful

asr-006022
06:42:47.580 --> 06:42:50.120
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: are the job opportunities

asr-006023
06:42:50.120 --> 06:42:52.080
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: that the department has been able to afford.

asr-006024
06:42:52.780 --> 06:42:54.340
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: I am a living witness kung how life-changing these programs are

asr-006025
06:42:54.340 --> 06:42:58.060
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: on how life-changing these programs are

asr-006026
06:42:58.060 --> 06:43:00.320
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: to individuals and their respective families.

asr-006027
06:43:01.240 --> 06:43:04.680
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: What in my mind used to be a political tool,

asr-006028
06:43:05.300 --> 06:43:06.980
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: meaning meant to assuage

asr-006029
06:43:06.980 --> 06:43:07.980
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: temporary jobs,

asr-006030
06:43:08.380 --> 06:43:10.840
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: temporary difficulties of families,

asr-006031
06:43:11.520 --> 06:43:13.980
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: are really lifeboats.

asr-006032
06:43:14.720 --> 06:43:16.320
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: They are important.

asr-006033
06:43:16.600 --> 06:43:19.160
Rep. Atty. Miro S. Quimbo: They come at a very critical time in their lives

asr-006034
06:43:19.160 --> 06:43:22.160
