07:51:40.590 --> 07:51:43.630
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: ah barely one inspector for forty thousand

asr-007673
07:51:43.630 --> 07:51:45.270
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: oh may hirap talaga iyon

asr-007674
07:51:45.270 --> 07:51:57.090
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: so pipilitin po natin madagdagan iyong mga inspectors basi po sa kanila qualifikasyon

asr-007675
07:51:57.090 --> 07:51:58.580
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: at examination results. Anything to add?

asr-007675-split-2
07:51:58.580 --> 07:52:06.830
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Dagdag ko lang po, Sec, na iyong ating mga labor inspectors ngayon, bukod doon

asr-007676
07:52:06.830 --> 07:52:08.650
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: sa those actually on field,

asr-007677
07:52:08.650 --> 07:52:18.010
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Meron din ho tayo dyan na mga kinukuha na labor inspection auditors to check on the work of our labor inspectors.

asr-007678
07:52:18.010 --> 07:52:24.410
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: At meron din dyan mga safety technical, technical safety inspectors.

asr-007679
07:52:24.550 --> 07:52:27.970
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Ito yung sa mga boilers, mechanical, and so on and so forth.

asr-007680
07:52:28.390 --> 07:52:34.210
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: At iba pa rin ho dyan, dahil kakulangan nila, yung iba rin ho dyan ay nag-hearing officer na rin.

asr-007681
07:52:34.670 --> 07:52:37.830
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: Pero right now, we are filling up all the items po.

asr-007682
07:52:37.830 --> 07:52:39.050
DOLE Assistant Secretary Amuerfina R. Reyes: So, thank you, Pop.

asr-007683
07:52:41.720 --> 07:52:43.700
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Did I hear that right, Asek?

asr-007684
07:52:44.120 --> 07:52:47.380
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: You are filling every position possible?

asr-007685
07:52:47.740 --> 07:52:48.000
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Tama ba?

asr-007686
07:52:48.300 --> 07:52:48.540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Okay.

asr-007687
07:52:48.540 --> 07:52:49.200
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you.

asr-007688
07:52:49.580 --> 07:52:56.100
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Now, for the final two questions, which are directly addressed to the secretaries of DOLE and TESDA.

asr-007689
07:52:56.500 --> 07:53:05.140
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: First, to Secretary Francis Tolentino, there's two questions, sir.

asr-007690
07:53:05.560 --> 07:53:08.280
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: A and B, I will read out first the first question.

asr-007691
07:53:08.820 --> 07:53:09.800
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: From FSL Nation.

asr-007692
07:53:09.820 --> 07:53:26.540
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: How was the department complied with previously and prospectively for 2027 for the mandate of RA 10524 on quotas for hiring on persons with disabilities, specifically deaf persons?

asr-007693
07:53:26.540 --> 07:53:39.460
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And kadugtongponon B is how many plantilia permanent other positions for deaf persons and FSL interpreters have been previously in the past years or prospectively appropriated?

asr-007694
07:53:39.820 --> 07:53:41.260
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: For 2027.

asr-007695
07:53:44.840 --> 07:53:48.600
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Persons with more longevity.

asr-007696
07:53:50.360 --> 07:53:50.680
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes.

asr-007697
07:53:51.200 --> 07:53:53.160
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yusek Warren, you're recognized.

asr-007698
07:53:53.160 --> 07:54:03.100
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: With the permission of the secretary, actually, sir, we do comply with the said Republic Act.

asr-007699
07:54:03.980 --> 07:54:09.380
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: And at the moment, we have in the central office two PWDs.

asr-007700
07:54:09.880 --> 07:54:12.420
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: These persons are given.

asr-007701
07:54:12.660 --> 07:54:14.480
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Equal opportunities for work.

asr-007702
07:54:14.860 --> 07:54:20.540
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: And if we have vacancies and they are being posted, everybody is welcome as long as qualified for the position.

asr-007703
07:54:21.120 --> 07:54:24.360
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: And for our regions, we'll probably get the data.

asr-007704
07:54:25.140 --> 07:54:25.860
DOLE Undersecretary Warren M. Miclat: Thank you, sir.

asr-007705
07:54:26.640 --> 07:54:30.860
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So the specific question, Yusek Warren, you said that there's two EWDs, right?

asr-007706
07:54:31.420 --> 07:54:36.120
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: But the question is if there are other positions for deaf persons.

asr-007707
07:54:36.120 --> 07:54:40.900
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Anyway, you can just give the data so that we can give the correct data to the committee secretary.

asr-007708
07:54:41.380 --> 07:54:42.640
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And we will give it to the CSOs.

asr-007709
07:54:42.660 --> 07:54:44.020
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: All right.

asr-007710
07:54:44.520 --> 07:54:47.820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And now for TESDA, final and last question.

asr-007711
07:54:48.680 --> 07:54:58.520
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: How much did your agency appropriate for 2026 for the FSL interpreting to make all your training programs accessible and inclusive for deaf clients?

asr-007712
07:54:59.160 --> 07:55:11.500
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Prospectively for 2027, following implementation of RA 12199, particularly for the training program for child development workers or ECCDs, has the IRR been issued?

asr-007713
07:55:12.660 --> 07:55:21.980
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: This is for, Mr. Chair, just for clarification, this is, again, for the training of the deaf, including for ECCD.

asr-007714
07:55:27.480 --> 07:55:28.100
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Mr. Chair?

asr-007715
07:55:30.530 --> 07:55:30.870
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Sorry.

asr-007716
07:55:33.330 --> 07:55:38.810
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: This is including for training of the deaf for ECCD as well.

asr-007717
07:55:39.170 --> 07:55:42.790
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: I'm sorry, I missed the, were there two parts to the question?

asr-007718
07:55:43.630 --> 07:55:48.870
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: The last part was prospectively for 2027, following implementation of RA 12199.

asr-007719
07:55:49.350 --> 07:55:57.590
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Particularly for the training program for child development workers for ECCDs, has the IRR been issued?

asr-007720
07:55:58.450 --> 07:56:01.110
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, I'll start with the second part.

asr-007721
07:56:01.330 --> 07:56:01.750
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Yes, go ahead.

asr-007722
07:56:01.750 --> 07:56:11.030
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So this is the IRR for the amendments to the ECCD law, and it has been signed into law.

asr-007723
07:56:11.410 --> 07:56:15.610
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, I mean, the IRR has actually been promulgated already.

asr-007724
07:56:16.910 --> 07:56:18.850
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: So, to the first question.

asr-007725
07:56:19.350 --> 07:56:33.330
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Sir, the training modules for the deaf has actually, for Filipino sign language, has actually been finished.

asr-007726
07:56:33.870 --> 07:56:44.670
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: And TESDA is now about to embark on the training of trainers, so that we can have as widespread infrastructure as possible for the training modules for Philippine sign language.

asr-007727
07:56:45.490 --> 07:56:46.430
TESDA Secretary Jose Francisco "Kiko" Benitez: Mr. Chair?

asr-007728
07:56:46.430 --> 07:56:48.830
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: Thank you, Secretary Kiko.

asr-007729
07:56:54.340 --> 07:57:05.820
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: So, Secretariat, ComSec, can you please gather all the data that was necessary for us to be able to furnish the CSOs that have been asking questions?

asr-007730
07:57:06.620 --> 07:57:09.500
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And for everyone's knowledge, that was the final question.

asr-007731
07:57:10.160 --> 07:57:21.740
Rep. Rommel Rico T. Angara: And I will just suspend our hearing, because when we return, I will relinquish my chair and give it to the Chairman of the Appropriations Committee.

asr-007732
08:00:20.050 --> 08:00:24.190
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Good evening po to our Dole family and TESDA family.

asr-007733
08:00:24.930 --> 08:00:32.730
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I wanted to be here to make sure this is the last committee hearing for this run of the budget cycle.

asr-007734
08:00:32.870 --> 08:00:37.190
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We just finished with DSWD and ito po ang ating grand finale.

asr-007735
08:00:37.930 --> 08:00:41.870
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It's the hearing of Dole and TESDA.

asr-007736
08:00:42.070 --> 08:00:45.290
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So that's why I wanted to make sure po to be here for the closing.

asr-007737
08:00:45.910 --> 08:00:48.090
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We wanted to say thank you po to everyone.

asr-007738
08:00:48.310 --> 08:00:49.310
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It's been a long day.

asr-007739
08:00:49.310 --> 08:00:52.690
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We started at 11 in the morning.

asr-007740
08:00:53.250 --> 08:00:54.530
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: It's 7.

asr-007741
08:00:55.030 --> 08:00:57.090
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So we've been running for 8 hours po.

asr-007742
08:00:57.150 --> 08:01:00.390
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So I don't want to lengthen the discussions further.

asr-007743
08:01:00.870 --> 08:01:10.390
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I think a lot of our colleagues raised a lot of the concerns, their commendation and all for Dole and TESDA.

asr-007744
08:01:10.990 --> 08:01:14.810
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And Kong Romel will be here with you po up until the plenary.

asr-007745
08:01:14.810 --> 08:01:18.410
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So whichever open items po are still pending,

asr-007746
08:01:18.410 --> 08:01:24.390
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: we'll work together po to be able to address those before the plenary.

asr-007747
08:01:25.030 --> 08:01:33.810
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And before I go any further, I would like to commend and say thank you to our budget sponsors who are here today.

asr-007748
08:01:34.330 --> 08:01:38.830
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you for your exemplary leadership in today's deliberations.

asr-007749
08:01:39.250 --> 08:01:43.330
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Of course, for the Dole family, Vice Chair Romel Angara,

asr-007750
08:01:43.810 --> 08:01:47.350
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and for the TESDA family, Vice Chair Angela Gila Garcia.

asr-007751
08:01:47.350 --> 08:01:48.250
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you.

asr-007752
08:01:48.250 --> 08:01:49.090
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much po.

asr-007753
08:01:49.210 --> 08:02:00.830
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We left you, Sec Kiko and Sec Tolentino, in very capable hands.

asr-007754
08:02:01.110 --> 08:02:07.990
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: They were the ones who also shepherded the passage of the budget of Dole and TESDA last year.

asr-007755
08:02:08.350 --> 08:02:11.050
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And by this year po, experts na sila.

asr-007756
08:02:11.250 --> 08:02:16.670
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So you are in very great hands with Vice Chair Angara and Vice Chair Garcia po.

asr-007757
08:02:16.670 --> 08:02:18.070
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: And siguro po, too.

asr-007758
08:02:18.070 --> 08:02:20.790
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So just to encapsulate today's discussions,

asr-007759
08:02:21.150 --> 08:02:29.050
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I wanted to give our secretaries the opportunity to, again,

asr-007760
08:02:29.890 --> 08:02:32.830
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: advocate for items that may need to be restored

asr-007761
08:02:32.830 --> 08:02:36.730
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: for the consideration of the Budget Amendments Review Subcommittee.

asr-007762
08:02:37.730 --> 08:02:45.430
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So siguro po, Secretary Tolentino, I have here the request letter from DOLE

asr-007763
08:02:45.430 --> 08:02:47.430
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: pertaining to the...

asr-007764
08:02:48.070 --> 08:02:53.150
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the additional allocation for TUPAD and GIP.

asr-007765
08:02:53.710 --> 08:02:57.790
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So SEC, if I may request you to please reiterate

asr-007766
08:02:57.790 --> 08:03:05.530
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the, perhaps, the implications of not being able to restore this back to the 2026 GAA level.

asr-007767
08:03:05.970 --> 08:03:13.630
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Because ang nangyari po, I saw in the NEP that instead of the 21 billion allocation

asr-007768
08:03:13.630 --> 08:03:16.430
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: as reflected in the 2026 GAA,

asr-007769
08:03:16.430 --> 08:03:20.570
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: sa 2027 na po, bumalik sa 11 billion.

asr-007770
08:03:20.850 --> 08:03:23.430
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So that represents a reduction of 10 billion peso.

asr-007771
08:03:23.630 --> 08:03:28.750
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So if you may please enlighten the committee as to the potential impact

asr-007772
08:03:28.750 --> 08:03:33.570
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: of not being able to restore this 10 billion pesos po in the [unclear].

asr-007773
08:03:34.690 --> 08:03:40.470
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: I think, Your Honor, that should be read in conjunction with the recently released

asr-007774
08:03:40.470 --> 08:03:46.230
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: labor force survey showing a decline in employment rate,

asr-007775
08:03:46.430 --> 08:03:57.690
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: as well as a, I think it's almost 2% increase in the labor force.

asr-007776
08:03:57.690 --> 08:04:09.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So the said programs initiated in that communication would address these gaps that,

asr-007777
08:04:09.160 --> 08:04:12.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: muntik na naman akong 'this representation',

asr-007778
08:04:12.820 --> 08:04:17.760
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: that this department feel would have to be continued.

asr-007779
08:04:17.960 --> 08:04:21.280
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: It is also very interesting, if we look at the GIP, the TUPAD,

asr-007780
08:04:22.100 --> 08:04:26.120
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: because of the uncertainties we're facing globally,

asr-007781
08:04:27.060 --> 08:04:32.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: even immediately after the U.S. midterm elections,

asr-007782
08:04:33.060 --> 08:04:38.820
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: science would show that the effects of the Iran war would still be there.

asr-007783
08:04:38.820 --> 08:04:45.740
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And we feel that the drastic decline, cut,

asr-007784
08:04:46.820 --> 08:04:47.820
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: to be sustained,

asr-007785
08:04:47.960 --> 08:04:56.500
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: to be imposed on the said program would be felt even in the countrysides.

asr-007786
08:04:57.260 --> 08:05:03.820
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: A while ago, we were talking about the tweaking, the innovation of the Tupad.

asr-007787
08:05:04.420 --> 08:05:07.800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We've seen a lot of improvement, especially in the education sector,

asr-007788
08:05:08.480 --> 08:05:14.460
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: wherein tutors, mentors are now being exposed via the Tupad program

asr-007789
08:05:14.460 --> 08:05:21.580
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: to increase the quality of education for grade 1, 2, and 3 pupils.

asr-007790
08:05:22.100 --> 08:05:28.920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We now see returning OFWs hand-in-hand with our partnership with TESDA through SECICO,

asr-007791
08:05:29.420 --> 08:05:32.580
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: the reintegration program, and a lot of other things.

asr-007792
08:05:32.580 --> 08:05:42.440
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: All these mechanisms would probably falter if we have a drastic decline

asr-007793
08:05:42.440 --> 08:05:44.440
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: in the allocation for the programs, Your Honor.

asr-007794
08:05:44.460 --> 08:05:46.460
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Iyon po siguro ang tenor ng naturang sulat.

asr-007795
08:05:46.460 --> 08:05:51.940
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Subalit kanina mayroon din akong request for

asr-007796
08:05:51.940 --> 08:05:59.420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Earlier, I also requested for an additional 125 million for labor justice.

asr-007797
08:05:59.420 --> 08:06:08.020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: It is only a small amount to fulfill the dream, not only for me but for others,

asr-007798
08:06:08.020 --> 08:06:14.100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: to have a strong academy, school, and finishing school.

asr-007799
08:06:14.100 --> 08:06:22.100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Our mediators, conciliators, arbiters, commissioners who provide justice for our workers.

asr-007800
08:06:22.100 --> 08:06:28.260
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: The same is the need to have more labor attorneys.

asr-007801
08:06:28.260 --> 08:06:30.880
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We have PAO now.

asr-007802
08:06:31.280 --> 08:06:37.540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Madam Chairperson, it is only 75 million, not a lot.

asr-007803
08:06:38.420 --> 08:06:43.580
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, all in all, I sent communications to Chairman,

asr-007804
08:06:44.100 --> 08:06:49.100
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Jolo, to the Speaker, and to Vice Chair Angara concerning this.

asr-007805
08:06:49.220 --> 08:06:56.180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: I consider labor justice as a primordial function of DOLE.

asr-007806
08:06:56.180 --> 08:07:03.260
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Bigyan ng karapat-dapat na karapatan, kilalanin ang manggagawang Pilipino

asr-007807
08:07:03.260 --> 08:07:11.440
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na itinuturing nating pawis ng Pilipino, puso ng bansa.

asr-007808
08:07:12.680 --> 08:07:13.540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Thank you very much.

asr-007809
08:07:14.100 --> 08:07:17.180
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much, Secretary Tolentino.

asr-007810
08:07:17.300 --> 08:07:20.840
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: If I may request for pertaining to the labor justice,

asr-007811
08:07:21.580 --> 08:07:26.080
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: if you may submit another letter, maybe containing both,

asr-007812
08:07:26.780 --> 08:07:35.140
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: the additional request for TUPAD amounting to 10.25 billion additional,

asr-007813
08:07:35.540 --> 08:07:43.260
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and then the 125 million as described by the Secretary pertaining to Labor Attorney's Office.

asr-007814
08:07:43.260 --> 08:07:44.060
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So, if...

asr-007815
08:07:44.100 --> 08:07:45.600
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We may request for both items.

asr-007816
08:07:45.740 --> 08:07:50.560
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Anything else, Sec, aside from the additional allocation for TUPAD

asr-007817
08:07:50.560 --> 08:07:54.860
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: and for the Labor Attorney's Office on the side of DOLE?

asr-007818
08:07:54.860 --> 08:07:56.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We will comply, Your Honor.

asr-007819
08:07:56.320 --> 08:07:58.660
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: We already have a copy of the folder.

asr-007820
08:08:01.660 --> 08:08:04.660
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Here it is, it's already up to you, your additional folder.

asr-007821
08:08:06.080 --> 08:08:11.040
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Your Honors, there are pending requests with...

asr-007822
08:08:11.880 --> 08:08:12.960
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: And this got the...

asr-007823
08:08:12.960 --> 08:08:15.040
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: This got the concurrence of the Department...

asr-007824
08:08:15.040 --> 08:08:16.080
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: of the Department of Labor.

asr-007825
08:08:16.280 --> 08:08:17.280
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: So, Foreign Affairs.

asr-007826
08:08:17.980 --> 08:08:24.360
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Sa darating puntaon, as I've mentioned earlier, early this afternoon,

asr-007827
08:08:24.360 --> 08:08:30.980
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: tayo po ang mamumuno ng International Labour Council ng ILO sa Geneva.

asr-007828
08:08:31.980 --> 08:08:38.600
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Simula po noon nawala yung puder sa Department of Employment

asr-007829
08:08:38.600 --> 08:08:43.440
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: at napunta sa Department of Migrant Workers iyong mga labor attach?s.

asr-007830
08:08:44.240 --> 08:08:45.180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Nangangailangan po,

asr-007831
08:08:45.180 --> 08:08:49.260
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: sa base sa mga liham na pinadala namin sa DBM,

asr-007832
08:08:49.680 --> 08:08:52.500
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na magkaroon man lang tayo ng kahit isang desk

asr-007833
08:08:52.500 --> 08:08:59.340
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na puwedeng magpagawa ng calling card na labor attach? sa Geneva.

asr-007834
08:09:00.440 --> 08:09:05.420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ganon din po sa Jakarta, kung saan tayo merong ASEAN Secretariat.

asr-007835
08:09:06.200 --> 08:09:09.540
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: At sa Washington, D.C., yung po yung tatlong hinihiling namin,

asr-007836
08:09:09.680 --> 08:09:14.180
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: hindi kalakihan, umaabot lang po ito sa aming pananaw,

asr-007837
08:09:14.180 --> 08:09:15.160
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: abunado pa sila.

asr-007838
08:09:15.180 --> 08:09:21.920
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: 137 milyon sa tatlong tao na ipoposte sa naturang tatlong lugar

asr-007839
08:09:21.920 --> 08:09:32.420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: to coordinate labor policy issues including maritime conventions among others

asr-007840
08:09:32.420 --> 08:09:35.040
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na sa ngayon po ay meron tayong void.

asr-007841
08:09:36.580 --> 08:09:39.420
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Isang desk lang po ang dadalin doon, isang tao,

asr-007842
08:09:39.960 --> 08:09:42.940
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: na meron naman sigurong subsistence allowance.

asr-007843
08:09:42.940 --> 08:09:43.020
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes.

asr-007844
08:09:44.060 --> 08:09:45.140
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Sabi ko nga doon,

asr-007845
08:09:45.180 --> 08:09:47.700
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: sa ambasador, doon na lang kahit matulog sa embahada,

asr-007846
08:09:48.180 --> 08:09:49.480
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: bigyan na lang ng kwarto doon.

asr-007847
08:09:49.660 --> 08:09:51.600
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yun lamang po, Madam Cherang Karagdagan.

asr-007848
08:09:52.760 --> 08:09:53.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Sec.

asr-007849
08:09:53.380 --> 08:09:55.020
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: We'll wait for the request.

asr-007850
08:09:55.140 --> 08:09:59.400
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: I don't know if the second folder already contained the ILO request.

asr-007851
08:10:00.540 --> 08:10:03.060
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So we'll just wait for those, Sec.

asr-007852
08:10:03.180 --> 08:10:07.760
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: If ever, if you may please give it to us by 12 noon tomorrow,

asr-007853
08:10:08.100 --> 08:10:13.560
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: given that we're targeting to convene the BARC at the soonest possible time.

asr-007854
08:10:13.560 --> 08:10:14.300
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: So we'll, we'll,

asr-007855
08:10:14.300 --> 08:10:18.780
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: just so we can have all of these under deliberation, po.

asr-007856
08:10:19.140 --> 08:10:20.300
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Yes, Your Honor, we'll submit.

asr-007857
08:10:20.300 --> 08:10:20.800
DOLE Secretary Francis N. Tolentino: Ugma.

asr-007858
08:10:21.220 --> 08:10:23.060
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you very much, po, Sec. Tolentino.

asr-007859
